Found in a bug hunt; reproduced and re-verified independently.

Cmd/Archive.pm:55 does

    my $id_str = $pos[0] or die "Usage: ...";

which passes, because "," is truthy. parse_ids(",") then splits to the empty
list, run_batch iterates nothing, and the command falls through to exit 0
with no output at all.

move, edit and delete all carry the guard that was added for exactly this
-- `die "Usage: ..." unless @ids;` at Move.pm:86, Edit.pm:193, Delete.pm:75,
each with a comment describing this precise failure. Archive was left out.

Reproduction:

    $ karr archive ,                      exit=0   (no output, nothing archived)
    $ karr archive ,, --json
    []                                    exit=0

    $ karr move , todo
    Usage: karr move ID[,ID,...] [STATUS]           exit=2
    $ karr edit , --title x
    Usage: karr edit ID[,ID,...] [FLAGS]            exit=2
    $ karr delete , --yes
    Usage: karr delete ID[,ID,...] [--yes] [--json]  exit=2

Cost: small but real -- a shell-built id list that comes out empty
(`karr archive "\$IDS"` with IDS=",") reports success for an archive that
never happened. ADR 0002 has no way to express "silently did nothing", which
is why the other three were fixed.
